- id: P:program/settle-the-answers
  type: program
  name: settle-the-answers
  summary: What a person said is written into the fabula, each answer where its question pointed, and nothing else
    in it moves.
  why: what a person said is written into the fabula, each answer where its question pointed, and nothing else in
    it moves.
  must: []
  decided:
  - date: 2026-11-05
    what: a second run, never a run that waits; "I don't know" leaves the field open in the person's own words.
  takes:
  - name: f
    type: fabula
  - name: said
    type: volume
  gives:
  - name: g
    type: fabula
  keeps:
  - only-the-asked
  lines: 3-15
  order: 1
  body: "program settle-the-answers\n  why: what a person said is written into the fabula, each answer where its\
    \ question pointed, and\n       nothing else in it moves.\n  decided 2026-11-05: a second run, never a run that\
    \ waits; \"I don't know\" leaves the field open\n       in the person's own words.\n\n  takes f: fabula, said:\
    \ volume\n  gives g: fabula\n  keeps only-the-asked against f\n\n  let answered = record said in f\n  give settle\
    \ answered\nend\n"
